   3182  fb8b							; PinSlot0 — with TWO candidates spanning two bands, slot 1 owns the highest
   3183  fb8b							; band, so slot 0 must be the OTHER one. Left to the rotation, the lower-band
   3184  fb8b							; object (the miner) was drawn only on 1 of 2 frames = flicker (user 2026-10-22).
   3185  fb8b							; SelectActiveObject does `inc FlickerFrame` then reduces it modulo the slot
   3186  fb8b							; count, so writing (desired + count - 1) makes the next frame land on
   3187  fb8b							; `desired` exactly. The bomb keeps its own 1-of-4 frames (skip while it is the
   3188  fb8b							; drawn object). In: FetchPtr+1 = max-Y candidate index ($FF = the miner),
   3189  fb8b							; Temp = its Y (unused here). Clobbers A.
