   3911  fe14							; ==============================================================================
   3912  fe14							; Phase 5 — second GRP1 object (no flicker). TIA has one GRP1 sprite, so two
   3913  fe14							; objects in a room used to alternate frames (30 Hz flicker each). When they
   3914  fe14							; live in DIFFERENT cave bands each can be drawn on ALL of its scanlines: the
   3915  fe14							; band's setup swaps the live trio (ObjBase/ObjTop/ActiveObjectX) for slot 1
   3916  fe14							; and repositions P1 there. The per-line object path is untouched — it already
   3917  fe14							; draws from the live trio and takes COLUP1 from ObjColorTab[ObjBase+row].
   3918  fe14							;
   3919  fe14							; Invariant (do not relax): slot 1's band is STRICTLY HIGHER than slot 0's.
   3920  fe14							; Bands are set up 0->1->2, so no later band has to restore slot 0's trio.
   3921  fe14							; Rooms whose two objects share a band keep the old behaviour (slot 0 only,
   3922  fe14							; rotation in SelectActiveObject unchanged).
   3923  fe14							; Cost: the band-compare early-out sits in the setup line's free tail (0
   3924  fe14							; lines); a band that DOES host slot 1 pays 2 lines (SetObjectXPos must start
   3925  fe14							; on a line boundary and the HMOVE needs the next line's HBLANK).
   3926  fe14							;
   3927  fe14							; StageSlot1 (VBLANK, after SelectActiveObject): stages ObjBase1/ObjTop1/ObjX1,
   3928  fe14							; $FF = none. Slot 1 = the miner or the first live enemy whose Y is in a band
   3929  fe14							; above slot 0's. The KEY skip mirrors the slot-0 path (KeyHeld = LevelStartRoom
   3930  fe14							; b7). Tally frames ($FE) are gated out: EnemyRamY holds score-pointer bytes
   3931  fe14							; then (AGENTS: tally frame draws the MINER only).
   3932  fe14							; ==============================================================================
   3933  fe14
