   3952  fe90							; FoldIndirect — cross-bank data fetch (HERO fold, write-triggered;
   3953  fe90							; level_bank_plan §0.1). Pad lands $FEF6-$FEFF (last byte ≤ $FEFF — $FF00
   3954  fe90							; stays the fineAdjust anchor). Bytes must be byte-identical in bank2
   3955  fe90							; (guard: verify_build) — after `sta $1FF8` the CPU fetches the remainder
   3956  fe90							; from the data bank at the same PC.
   3957  fe90							; Contract: bank select is ABSOLUTE $1FF8 (bank2) — X/Y both preserved,
   3958  fe90							; A = junk in, data out (`sta $1FF6` switches back, A preserved).
   3959  fe90							; P3.1 deviation (plan §0): `sta $1FF8,X` required X=0, but every enemy
   3960  fe90							; loop keeps the slot in X and has no free temp to swap (DEY/snake hold
   3961  fe90							; Temp live across the read). All level data is bank2, so X-selection is
   3962  fe90							; dead weight; bank3 data later needs a second entry `sta $1FF9` pad.
   3963  fe90							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   3964  fe90							; E4 moth entry tramp ($FEF0-$FEF5) — byte-identical with bank2's copy
   3965  fe90							; (guard: verify_build check_moth_tramp). bank0 executes `sta $1FF8`; the next
   3966  fe90							; fetch ($FEF3) comes from bank2 = `jmp MothRoutine`. Neither bank runs its
   3967  fe90							; other half: bank0 is switched away at $FEF2, bank2 is never entered here.
   3968  fe90							; The 6-byte pad is the only free hole before FoldIndirect's pinned $FEF6.
   3969  fe90							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
